            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "This disables section GC for all targets, including Windows and wasm32, but the PR description says Windows is left untouched and the reported dead-stripping issue is macOS-specific (#40622). Consider gating this to Darwin (or otherwise aligning the code change with the stated scope), so other platforms keep their existing linker GC behavior.",
            "commit_id": "5e902f9402dd5e1fcb45db29d76827973f722add",
            "created_at": "2026-08-15T04:28:38Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -498,6 +498,10 @@ pub fn build(b: *std.Build) !void {\n         .root_module = nvim_mod,\n     }) else b.addExecutable(.{ .name = \"nvim\", .root_module = nvim_mod });\n     nvim_exe.rdynamic = true; // -E\n+    // Native Lua modules resolve Lua C API symbols from the nvim executable, so\n+    // symbols must be kept even when nothing inside nvim references them. On\n+    // macOS the linker dead-strips them before rdynamic exports them. #40622\n+    nvim_exe.link_gc_sections = false;",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41320#discussion_r3788485927",
