            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "The description was inconsistent with the diff — fixed, thanks. The change is intentionally unconditional.\n\nOn wasm32: this is a no-op. The wasm target is built as a static library (`addLibrary(.{ .linkage = .static })`), and `--no-gc-sections` does not affect archive creation. With zig 0.16.0 the produced `.a` is byte-identical with and without it. `x86_64-windows-gnu` also builds unchanged.\n\nOn gating to Darwin: deliberately not done. #40624 was closed precisely because it encoded a per-platform, per-symbol policy — the request was that _all_ non-`static` symbols be exported on every supported platform. Gating this on Darwin would reintroduce the same objection.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
            "commit_id": "5e902f9402dd5e1fcb45db29d76827973f722add",
            "created_at": "2026-08-15T04:47:53Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -498,6 +498,10 @@ pub fn build(b: *std.Build) !void {\n         .root_module = nvim_mod,\n     }) else b.addExecutable(.{ .name = \"nvim\", .root_module = nvim_mod });\n     nvim_exe.rdynamic = true; // -E\n+    // Native Lua modules resolve Lua C API symbols from the nvim executable, so\n+    // symbols must be kept even when nothing inside nvim references them. On\n+    // macOS the linker dead-strips them before rdynamic exports them. #40622\n+    nvim_exe.link_gc_sections = false;",
